"""Dependency-free static, privacy-safe public dashboard builder."""
import json, html
from pathlib import Path
D=json.loads(Path('data/evidence.json').read_text())
e=html.escape
nav=[('index','Executive summary')]+[(p['id'],p['title']) for p in D['pages']]+[('sources','Sources & methodology'),('dashboard/index','Category dashboard')]
def shell(id,title,content):
    return f'''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><meta name="description" content="Privacy-safe, evidence-linked Los Angeles net lease property research. Unknown financial values are withheld."><title>{e(title)} · Asset A · Net-lease decision file</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="assets/style.css"></head><body><a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a><aside><a class="brand" href="index.html"><span class="mark">A.</span> ASSET A<span class="brand-sub">NET-LEASE DECISION FILE</span></a><div class="nav-label">DECISION WORKSPACE</div><nav>{''.join(f'<a {"aria-current=page" if key==id else ""} href="{key}.html"><span>{str(i+1).zfill(2)}</span>{e(label)}</a>' for i,(key,label) in enumerate(nav))}</nav><div class="privacy"><span>◈</span><b>Privacy by design</b><p>Asset A · anonymized<br>No owner or parcel identifiers</p></div></aside><div class="workspace"><header><span>RESEARCH / LOS ANGELES</span><span class="stamp">● &nbsp; Evidence snapshot · {D["reviewed"]}</span></header><main id="main"><section class="callout"><b>Evidence boundary.</b> Asset A is anonymized: no address, parcel, owner or executed lease is published. No valuation, cap rate or sale price is asserted. Companion research layers are kept in the repository but withheld from this site, including the <code>/advisory/</code> projections. <a href="review.html">Flagged for Review</a>.</section>{content}</main><footer>Independent decision-support research. Not an appraisal, legal opinion or personalized financial advice.<br>Static evidence snapshot · No tracking, forms, third-party assets or private documents · <a href="sources.html">Methodology &amp; limitations</a></footer></div></body></html>'''
def table(p):
    heads=p['columns']+['Evidence','Official source']
    out='<div class="table-wrap"><table><caption>'+e(p['title'])+' · evidence register</caption><thead><tr>'+''.join('<th scope="col">'+e(c)+'</th>' for c in heads)+'</tr></thead><tbody>'
    for r in p['rows']:
        s=D['sources'][r['source']]; status=r['status']; cls='verified' if status=='Verified' else 'analysis' if status=='Analysis' else 'unknown'
        out+='<tr>'+''.join('<td'+(' class="empty" aria-label="Unverified value; intentionally blank"' if c=='' else '')+'>'+e(c)+'</td>' for c in r['cells'])+f'<td><span class="badge {cls}">{e(status)}</span></td><td><a href="{e(s["url"])}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{e(s["label"])} ↗</a></td></tr>'
    return out+'</tbody></table></div>'
for p in D['pages']:
    intro=f'<div class="eyebrow">{e(p["kicker"])}</div><h1>{e(p["title"])}</h1><p class="lede">{e(p["description"])}</p><div class="legend"><span class="badge verified">Verified</span> Source-matched observation <span class="badge analysis">Analysis</span> Conditional interpretation <span class="badge unknown">Unverified</span> Missing evidence</div>'
    Path(p['id']+'.html').write_text(shell(p['id'],p['title'],intro+table(p)))
content='''<div class="eyebrow">ASSET A · CENTRAL LOS ANGELES · NET-LEASE DECISION FILE</div><h1>Protect the income.<br><span>Own the exit.</span></h1><p class="lede">A source-linked decision file for an anonymized Jack in the Box net-leased restaurant property reported to expire between 2030 and 2035. Every published figure is traceable to a government or issuer page; everything that could not be verified is left blank and listed on the review page.</p><div class="hero-note"><span class="badge analysis">CONDITIONAL RECOMMENDATION · ANALYST JUDGEMENT, NOT A VALUATION</span><h2>Run both tracks now: market the asset for sale, and demand renewal terms in writing.</h2><p>Start a confidential sale process 24–36 months before the earliest expiry, in parallel with a written renewal request. Convert to whichever result the documents support: a verified after-tax sale, or an enforceable extension of ten years or more at market rent with acceptable credit. What is not defensible is letting a 2030–2035 option clock run out on regional averages alone.</p><a class="button" href="decisions.html">Decision pathways &amp; triggers <span>→</span></a><a class="quiet" href="taxes.html">After-tax cost of each route ↗</a></div><section class="split"><div><div class="eyebrow">WHY NOW RATHER THAN AT EXPIRY</div><h2>Every verified trend is flat or negative.</h2><p>City population is 0.8% below its 2020 estimates base and the county is 3.2% below. Metro payrolls grew 0.5% year over year, led by education and health while information fell 5.7%. The tenant reports system same-store sales of −1.1% and is closing 150–200 restaurants, with the remainder tied to franchise-agreement termination dates.</p><p>An expiring lease transfers negotiating leverage to the party that can wait. Marketing while income is contractual, and while the tenant still needs the site, is the lower-risk way to preserve capital.</p></div><div class="callout"><h3>What would change this view</h3><p>A signed extension at market rent backed by acceptable credit; a verified after-tax bid above the hold case; block-level evidence that this trade area is growing; or a change in the owner's liquidity needs.</p><p><b>None of these can be established from the regional data published here.</b> The property's rent, basis, debt and lease are not public records we hold.</p><a href="review.html">Inspect the evidence gaps →</a></div></section><div class="section-heading"><h2>The evidence in three numbers</h2><span>Regional context ≠ property forecast</span></div><div class="cards"><article><div class="eyebrow">DEMAND / LA CITY</div><strong>−0.8%</strong><p>Population change, April 2020 estimates base to July 2025. A demand headwind, not a local sales forecast.</p><a href="https://www.census.gov/quickfacts/losangelescitycalifornia">Census · V2025 ↗</a></article><article><div class="eyebrow">JOBS / LA METRO</div><strong>+0.5%</strong><p>Nonfarm employment, September 2026 versus September 2025, not seasonally adjusted. Growth is thinner than inflation.</p><a href="https://www.bls.gov/regions/west/summary/blssummary_losangeles.pdf">BLS · November 2026 summary ↗</a></article><article><div class="eyebrow">TENANT / CHAIN-WIDE</div><strong>−1.1%</strong><p>System same-store sales, third quarter FY2026. This is not the subject restaurant's performance and not the guarantor's rent coverage.</p><a href="tenant.html">Issuer evidence &amp; lease gaps ↗</a></article></div><div class="section-heading"><h2>Risk balance</h2><span>Business as usual, then the tail</span></div><section class="split"><div><h2 style="font-size:19px">Business as usual</h2><p><b>Income concentration.</b> One tenant, one building, one lease. A vacancy costs the full rent, plus taxes, insurance and re-letting.</p><p><b>Wage and cost pressure.</b> Covered fast-food work pays $20.00/hour under AB 1228, and the state floor is $16.90/hour from 2026. Rent coverage at the store level is unknown.</p><p><b>Rates and exit yields.</b> The 10-year Treasury was 4.84% on 5 November 2026. A higher exit yield lowers price for the same rent.</p>
<p><b>Schools.</b> Los Angeles Unified graduates 86.5% of its four-year cohort (2025 Dashboard), a district-wide outcome that says nothing about the campus assigned to any one site.</p><p><b>Taxes.</b> A city sale above $5.4m carries a 4% Measure ULA surcharge on top of the 0.45% city base tax; the county charges $0.55 per $500 and bills the full $1.10 per $1,000 inside Los Angeles; §1031 defers, and does not eliminate, capital-gain tax.</p></div><div><h2 style="font-size:19px">Tail events that can end the local economy</h2><p><b>Wildfire.</b> In 2025 the Palisades and Eaton fires destroyed 16,264 structures in this county in 24 days. Insurance availability and pricing can change for the whole region afterwards.</p><p><b>Earthquake.</b> USGS models a plausible M7.8 southern San Andreas event at ~1,800 deaths and ~$213bn in losses. Parcel-level ground-failure exposure has not been checked.</p><p><b>Flood, and correlated utility or pandemic disruption.</b> The FEMA map service is the official source; no parcel zone has been assigned.</p><p><b>Tenant failure or accelerated closure.</b> The issuer's own programme closes underperforming units and sells owned real estate. Neither establishes this site's fate, but both remove the assumption that a chain lease is permanent.</p><a href="risk.html">Read the full risk register →</a></div></section><div class="section-heading"><h2>Page directory</h2><span>Twelve pages · every row carries its source and its status</span></div><div class="table-wrap"><table><caption>Every page on this site, with how many sourced rows it holds</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">#</th><th scope="col">Page</th><th scope="col">Category</th><th scope="col">Sourced rows</th><th scope="col">Read it</th><th scope="col">Most-cited official source on the page</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>01</td><td>Area fundamentals</td><td>Regional evidence</td><td>23</td><td><a href="economy.html">Open Area fundamentals →</a></td><td><a href="https://www.bls.gov/regions/west/summary/blssummary_losangeles.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">BLS · LA economic summary</a></td></tr><tr><td>02</td><td>Trade area &amp; demographics</td><td>DEMAND / DEMOGRAPHICS</td><td>14</td><td><a href="demographics.html">Open Trade area &amp; demographics →</a></td><td><a href="https://www.census.gov/quickfacts/losangelescitycalifornia" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">U.S. Census · LA city</a></td></tr><tr><td>03</td><td>Tenant &amp; lease</td><td>Income durability</td><td>18</td><td><a href="tenant.html">Open Tenant &amp; lease →</a></td><td><a href="https://investors.jackinthebox.com/news/news-details/2026/Jack-in-the-Box-Inc--Reports-Third-Quarter-2026-Earnings/default.aspx" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Issuer · Q3 FY2026 results</a></td></tr><tr><td>04</td><td>Risk &amp; resilience</td><td>Downside first</td><td>12</td><td><a href="risk.html">Open Risk &amp; resilience →</a></td><td><a href="https://msc.fema.gov/portal/home" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">FEMA · flood maps</a></td></tr><tr><td>05</td><td>Neighborhood &amp; land</td><td>Location matters</td><td>6</td><td><a href="place.html">Open Neighborhood &amp; land →</a></td><td><a href="https://zimas.lacity.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">LA City Planning · ZIMAS</a></td></tr><tr><td>06</td><td>Schools &amp; workforce</td><td>HUMAN CAPITAL / SCHOOLS</td><td>7</td><td><a href="schools.html">Open Schools &amp; workforce →</a></td><td><a href="https://www.cde.ca.gov/sdprofile/details.aspx?cds=19647330000000" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CDE · LAUSD district profile</a></td></tr><tr><td>07</td><td>Decision pathways</td><td>Conditional strategy</td><td>10</td><td><a href="decisions.html">Open Decision pathways →</a></td><td><a href="https://www.irs.gov/businesses/small-businesses-self-employed/like-kind-exchanges-real-estate-tax-tips" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">IRS · like-kind exchanges</a></td></tr><tr><td>08</td><td>Taxes &amp; transaction costs</td><td>AFTER TAX / TRANSACTION COSTS</td><td>18</td><td><a href="taxes.html">Open Taxes &amp; transaction costs →</a></td><td><a href="https://assessor.lacounty.gov/real-estate-toolkit/proposition-13" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">LA County Assessor · Proposition 13</a></td></tr><tr><td>09</td><td>Projection framework</td><td>No invented forecasts</td><td>9</td><td><a href="model.html">Open Projection framework →</a></td><td><a href="https://investors.jackinthebox.com/news/news-details/2026/Jack-in-the-Box-Inc--Reports-Third-Quarter-2026-Earnings/default.aspx" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Issuer · Q3 FY2026 results</a></td></tr><tr><td>10</td><td>Flagged for Review</td><td>Transparent limitations</td><td>26</td><td><a href="review.html">Open Flagged for Review →</a></td><td><a href="https://investors.jackinthebox.com/news/news-details/2026/Jack-in-the-Box-Inc--Reports-Third-Quarter-2026-Earnings/default.aspx" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Issuer · Q3 FY2026 results</a></td></tr><tr><td>11</td><td>Sources &amp; methodology</td><td>Audit trail</td><td>26</td><td><a href="sources.html">Open sources →</a></td><td><a href="https://www.census.gov/quickfacts/losangelescitycalifornia" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">U.S. Census · LA city</a></td></tr><tr><td>12</td><td>Category dashboard</td><td>Second, independently built view</td><td>185</td><td><a href="dashboard/index.html">Open dashboard →</a></td><td><a href="https://www.bls.gov/regions/west/summary/blssummary_losangeles.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">BLS · LA economic summary</a></td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class="section-heading"><h2>Read by category</h2><span>Twelve pages · every row carries its source</span></div><div class="route-grid"><a href="economy.html"><b>Area fundamentals</b><p>Population, income, payrolls, prices and wages.</p>Read the evidence →</a><a href="demographics.html"><b>Trade area &amp; demographics</b><p>Households, age, poverty and spending capacity.</p>Read the evidence →</a><a href="tenant.html"><b>Tenant &amp; lease</b><p>Issuer results, closures and the missing lease.</p>Read the evidence →</a><a href="risk.html"><b>Risk &amp; resilience</b><p>Business-as-usual and black-swan events.</p>Review downside →</a><a href="place.html"><b>Neighborhood &amp; land</b><p>What cannot be said without a parcel.</p>Inspect gaps →</a><a href="schools.html"><b>Schools &amp; workforce</b><p>District scale, enrollment, missing measures.</p>Read the evidence →</a><a href="taxes.html"><b>Taxes &amp; transaction costs</b><p>Prop 13, transfer taxes, ULA, §1031, gains.</p>Model the net →</a><a href="decisions.html"><b>Decision pathways</b><p>Six routes, their triggers and their risks.</p>Compare routes →</a><a href="model.html"><b>Projection framework</b><p>Verified anchors, and the forecasts withheld.</p>See the limits →</a></div>'''

Path('index.html').write_text(shell('index','Executive summary',content))
src={'title':'Official source register','columns':['Publisher / document','Type','Reviewed','Use and limits'],'rows':[dict(cells=[s['label'],s['type'],s['checked'],'Primary source checked for published observations; not a property appraisal.'],status='Verified',source=k) for k,s in D['sources'].items()]}
content='''<div class="eyebrow">08 / AUDIT TRAIL</div><h1>Sources &amp; methodology</h1><p class="lede">Evidence first. Interpretation second. Unknowns stay unknown.</p><section class="callout"><h2>Verification standard</h2><p>Verified rows are source-matched observations re-read from the publisher page on 8 November 2026, and the headline figures were re-read again on 10 November 2026; the row-by-row records are <code>research/VERIFICATION-2026-11-10.md</code>, <code>research/VERIFICATION-2026-11-10-882bff85.md</code> and, for the prior snapshot, <code>research/VERIFICATION-2026-11-08.md</code> in the repository. Department of Education district data for Los Angeles Unified was also read; no school attendance boundary can be assigned to an unidentified parcel. A link is not a guarantee that a rolling source will retain an earlier value. Verified means the source reports the observation—not that it predicts this property. Issuer reports are labeled separately from government data.</p><p>Analysis rows are our conditional reasoning. Their official links support background context only; they do not endorse the recommendation. Unverified rows contain no invented value; links are research routes or explicitly limited context, not proof of missing facts.</p><p>QuickFacts observations use different vintages, geography and survey periods. ACS estimates have sampling error; no tract estimates or margins of error were obtained. The BLS November 4, 2026 summary uses unadjusted data and may be revised. Hazard context is drawn from USGS scenario modelling and CAL FIRE incident records, not from parcel-level analysis. No model has been trained or back-tested; no causal claim about property value is made.</p><h3>Privacy and publication boundary</h3><p>Asset A and Owner A are placeholders. No addresses, parcel IDs, owner names, contact details, financial accounts or private lease records are collected or published. No analytics, third-party embeds or external scripts are used. GitHub hosting may retain standard access logs. Public source links open their publishers’ websites.</p><h3>Reproducibility and maintenance</h3><p>Public evidence is stored in data/evidence.json; scripts/build.py generates every page. scripts/validate.py checks table provenance, local links and blank-value status. Source values were reviewed manually; automated validation does not assert live external availability or semantic verification. This is a fixed snapshot, not a live data feed. Refresh official releases and reassess geographic fit before acting.</p><p>Earlier companion reports, including the <code>/advisory/</code> layer and its numerical projections, are retained in the repository but excluded from this public site pending independent validation; see Flagged for Review. No hidden property records or private evidence were inferred. Missing private documents cannot be supplied through autonomous public research.</p></section>'''+table(src)
Path('sources.html').write_text(shell('sources','Sources & methodology',content))
